<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<%- include('../partials/breadcrumbs') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>About <%= brand %></h1>
    <p>Who runs this catalogue, what is actually in it, and what this site will not tell you.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>What <%= brand %> is</h2>
    <p>
      <%= brand %> is the online catalogue of a licensed firearms dealer trading in the state of
      <%= jurisdiction.stateOrRegion %>. It lists <%= stats.total %> Glock pistols, slides and triggers,
      across <%= stats.modelCount %> models, with <%= stats.nineMm %> of those listings chambered in 9mm.
      Everything on it is stock the shop holds a record for. It is not a marketplace, not a dropshipping
      front and not an affiliate site.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site processes secure payments and ships to your pickup location. For firearms, your pickup location must be a licensed dealer who completes ATF Form 4473 and the background check. You place an order, pay securely, and the transfer happens under the process on the
      <a href="/shipping-and-transfer-policy">shipping and transfer page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How the shop operates</h2>
    <p>
      Every firearm sold here is transferred through a licensed dealer at your pickup location, with
      <%= jurisdiction.transactionRecordForm %> completed at the counter and a background check run through
      the <%= jurisdiction.backgroundCheckSystem %> before anything is released. The minimum age from a
      licensed dealer is <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeHandgun %> for a handgun and
      <%= jurisdiction.minimumAgeLongGun %> for a rifle or shotgun. Texas sets no waiting period, no
      purchase permit and no state registration, but the federal check still runs on every transfer. The
      full detail, including what happens if you live outside Texas, is on the
      <a href="/compliance">compliance page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What is in the catalogue</h2>
    <p>
      <%= stats.total %> listings across <%= stats.modelCount %> Glock models, covering factory
      configurations, factory colored finishes, custom slide and grip work, optic ready builds, spare slides
      and drop in triggers. Prices run from $<%= money(stats.minPrice) %> to $<%= money(stats.maxPrice) %>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The deepest inventory is in the compact and subcompact frames. If you are looking for a specific
      model, the <a href="/models">model index</a> lists every one with its count, and the
      <a href="/calibers">caliber index</a> cuts the same stock the other way.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Every listing on this site is generated from the shop's own stock export. The caliber, barrel length,
      magazine capacity, SKU, price and availability shown on a product page are the values held in that
      record. Where a field is missing from the record, the product page leaves it out instead of filling it
      with a plausible number. Barrel length is present for a little over half the source rows and capacity
      for rather fewer, so you will see product pages with short specification tables. That is the data
      being honest rather than the page being broken.
    </p>

    <h2>Marketing copy</h2>
    <p>
      The supplier export arrived with promotional descriptions attached. That copy made claims the shop
      cannot evidence, so none of it was published. Product pages carry the specification table and a factual
      one line summary until the shop writes descriptions it can stand behind.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It is not affiliated with Glock Ges.m.b.H. GLOCK is their registered trademark.</li>
      <li>It does not publish customer reviews or ratings, because none have been collected. No rating markup is sent to search engines either.</li>
      <li>It does not complete a firearm transfer online. The final transfer is completed in person at your pickup location.</li>
      <li>It does not publish a specification, a delivery estimate or a fee that the shop cannot stand behind.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> for stock questions, transfer questions or anything the
      product pages do not answer. Replies come from a person, not an automated system.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
